    intro: 'In the spring of 2020, with schools shut and whole countries told to stay at home, a lot of people did something that would once have been described as antisocial: they played more video games. Parents who had spent years rationing screen time sat down on the sofa with their children and a console. Friends who could not meet in a pub met on an island in Animal Crossing. Researchers noticed, and in the two years that followed they published a small but useful body of peer-reviewed work on what that play actually did for people. The findings are more mixed than the cheerful headlines of the time, and more interesting.',
