          'When the researchers sorted the free-text answers, seven themes came out, including cognitive stimulation, reduced anxiety and stress, a sense of escape and, prominently, opportunities to socialise. People described games as a place to keep up friendships that had nowhere else to go: a weekly session with old university friends, a regular match with a sibling in another city.',
